---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";

const sections = [
  ["introduction", "Introduction"],
  ["reporting", "Reporting security issues"],
  ["research", "Responsible research"],
  ["responsibilities", "Your responsibilities"],
] as const;
---

<LegalPage
  title="Security Policy | O3 Code"
  description="How to report security vulnerabilities in O3 Code privately."
  heading="O3 Code Security Policy"
  lede="Report vulnerabilities privately so maintainers can investigate without exposing users to unnecessary risk."
  effectiveDate="2026-11-03"
  lastUpdated="2026-11-03"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="introduction">
    <p class="section-number">01</p>
    <h2>Introduction</h2>
    <p>
      This policy covers the O3 Code project at{" "}<a
        href="https://github.com/owenqwenstarsky/o3code">owenqwenstarsky/o3code</a
      >. O3 Code connects clients to environments and coding-agent providers you configure.
      Operators are responsible for securing their own instances, environments, and credentials.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="reporting">
    <p class="section-number">02</p>
    <h2>Reporting Security Issues</h2>
    <p>
      Report suspected vulnerabilities through{" "}<a
        href="https://github.com/owenqwenstarsky/o3code/security/advisories/new"
        >GitHub private vulnerability reporting</a
      >. Avoid public issues or discussions for undisclosed vulnerabilities.
    </p>
    <p>Please include, when available:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>A description of the issue and its potential impact;</li>
      <li>The affected version and component;</li>
      <li>Reproduction steps or a minimal proof of concept; and</li>
      <li>Relevant logs or screenshots with secrets and personal information removed.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Use the private report to discuss investigation and disclosure with maintainers.
      This project does not promise a response or resolution deadline.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="research">
    <p class="section-number">03</p>
    <h2>Responsible Research</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Test only systems, accounts, and data you own or have explicit permission to test;</li>
      <li>Access only the information needed to demonstrate the issue;</li>
      <li>Stop if you encounter other people's private data;</li>
      <li>Avoid disrupting availability or damaging or deleting data; and</li>
      <li>Do not test third-party providers or services without their permission.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="responsibilities">
    <p class="section-number">04</p>
    <h2>Your Responsibilities</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Keep O3 Code, your operating systems, and connected tools up to date;</li>
      <li>Secure your instances, devices, environments, repositories, networks, and backups;</li>
      <li>Protect credentials and revoke any that may have been exposed;</li>
      <li>Grant providers and integrations only the permissions they need; and</li>
      <li>Review agent commands and source changes before applying them.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Never include passwords, API keys, access tokens, or private keys in a report.</p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
